MINI SOCIAL NETWORK PROJECT

A Comprehensive Analysis and Implementation Study

ABSTRACT

This project presents the development and implementation of a Mini Social Network platform using Django web framework. The system provides users with the ability to create profiles, post content, interact through likes and comments, and access analytics dashboard for platform insights. The project demonstrates the application of modern web development technologies including Django, Bootstrap, Chart.js, and SQLite database management. The platform features user authentication, real-time content sharing, social interactions, and comprehensive analytics visualization. The implementation showcases best practices in web application development, database design, and user experience optimization. The analytics module provides valuable insights into user engagement patterns, content performance, and platform growth metrics through interactive charts and statistical analysis.

Keywords: Social Network, Django, Web Development, User Analytics, Content Management, Social Media Platform

